        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(workboard): prevent custom select menu flash to top-left before positioning",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen clicking a custom `<details>`-based select (status, priority, agent, session) inside the workboard card modal, the dropdown menu briefly flashes at the viewport origin before jumping to the correct position.\n\nRoot cause: `positionWorkboardSelectMenu` computes and applies CSS custom properties synchronously during `@toggle`, but the menu's CSS default (`top: 0; left: 0`) may be painted for one frame before the JS-delivered values take effect.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSet `visibility: hidden` as the menu's default CSS state. After positioning values are applied, toggle `visibility: visible` in the same synchronous handler.\n\n`visibility: hidden` keeps the element in layout so `getBoundingClientRect` returns correct measurements, unlike `display: none` which would remove it from layout entirely.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCustom select dropdowns in the workboard card-modal form now appear directly at their correct position with no flash.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Existing regression tests\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/workboard/view.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  70 passed (70)\n```\n\n### After fix\n\n<img width=\"600\" alt=\"workboard select after fix\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c60cfa0e-7485-4426-ac7b-783fe9c47a11\" />\n\n### Fix invariants\n\n| State | CSS | Effect |\n|-------|-----|--------|\n| Default (closed) | `display: none` + `visibility: hidden` | Not in layout, not painted |\n| `[open]` fires | `display: grid` (CSS) + `visibility: hidden` (inline) | In layout, not painted |\n| After positioning | `--top`/`--left` set + `visibility: visible` | In layout, painted at correct position |\n| Close | `display: none` + `visibility: hidden` | Reset for next open |\n\n### Files Changed (2 files, +3 lines)\n\n```\n ui/src/pages/workboard/view.ts | 2 ++\n ui/src/styles/workboard.css    | 1 +\n```",
